    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2WCDZsDJ9sgBpcwvxPEonRo)_\n\n## What\nA global hotkey pops a small floating box; you type `Buy milk #errands !fri` and press Return. A `** TODO` (with `:ID:`, `:CREATED:`, tag and `DEADLINE`) lands under \"Tasks\" in `inbox.org` and you are back in the app you were in.\n\n- Inline syntax: `#tag` (matched against `org-tag-alist` and the tag registry, `#err` finds `@errands`, TAB completes), `!date` deadline, `^date` scheduled. Dates: `today`, `tom`, `fri`, `+3d`, `2w`, `3nov`, `2026-11-03`.\n- Live preview under the prompt shows title, tags and dates, and warns about unknown or ambiguous tags and bad dates.\n- Two entry points: `tools/quick-capture` (`emacsclient -e '(sp-quick-capture-popup)'`) and `org-protocol://sp-quick-capture[?text=…]` (with `text` it captures silently, for Alfred/Raycast/Shortcuts input fields).\n- Module `sp-quick-capture` loads right after `sp-org-capture`; the doc has the macOS setup steps for Raycast, Alfred, Hammerspoon, skhd and Shortcuts.\n\n## Verified\n`tests/sp-quick-capture-test.el`: 8 ERT tests (dates, tag matching, parser, writing into a new and an existing heading) pass in Emacs 29.3 batch. Byte-compiles clean.\n\n## Not tested (no macOS/GUI Emacs here)\nThe frame (`make-frame` from a daemon with the `ns` window system, centring, focus), the preview overlay, interaction with `mini-frame`, hiding Emacs afterwards (`ns-do-hide-emacs`), the `org-protocol://` URL handler registration and the hotkey itself.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nv18Dts2Bw3SSBDEV1kzyy)_",
